=== the source's own contract, verbatim ===
11:const unsigned long long MAX_SIZE = 1000000;  /// variable upto which prime numbers are to be found out
39: * @param size denotes upto which prime numbers are to be found out
59:    const int size = 10; /* array size */

=== measurement on the real prime array ===
indices:  0=0 1=0 2=1 3=1 5=1 7=1 10=0 11=1 13=1
count(arr,3       ) = 2       first 3        elements = 1       DIFFER
count(arr,7       ) = 4       first 7        elements = 3       DIFFER
count(arr,10      ) = 4       first 10       elements = 4       same
count(arr,11      ) = 5       first 11       elements = 4       DIFFER
count(arr,13      ) = 6       first 13       elements = 5       DIFFER
count(arr,97      ) = 25      first 97       elements = 24      DIFFER
count(arr,1000000 ) = 78498   first 1000000  elements = 78498   same

=== reading of the result ===
count(arr, 10) = 4 and the exclusive reading is also 4 -> the test value (10)
cannot distinguish the two readings, because 10 is not prime. The two readings
differ exactly when size is itself prime (3, 7, 11, 13, 97 above).
Verdict: ambiguous contract, NOT a confirmed defect.
